# Homestead — deployment reference, template
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so keep
# every value here a placeholder. Never paste a real token into this file.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing in the project reads either file. The deploy runs on GitHub Actions
# and takes its credentials from repository secrets. This exists so the values
# are on hand — to re-add a secret, deploy by hand, or call the Cloudflare API.


# ── Cloudflare ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Cloudflare → My Profile → API Tokens → Create Token →
#   "Edit Cloudflare Workers" template → Use template
#
# The stock template is sufficient as-is; no permissions need adding. There is
# no separate Durable Objects permission — the DO migration ships as part of the
# script upload, which `Workers Scripts → Edit` already covers.
#
# Scope Account Resources to your own account rather than "All accounts". Set
# Zone Resources to "All zones" if you may add a custom domain later.
#
# Shown once on creation. Rotate at API Tokens → Roll, and update the matching
# GitHub secret or the deploy will start failing.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=cfut_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Cloudflare → Compute → Workers & Pages → Account Details → Account ID.
# An identifier rather than a secret.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=0000000000000000000000000000000

# Created automatically the first time you open Compute → Workers & Pages.
# Until it exists, `wrangler deploy` refuses to publish. Not a secret.
CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS_SUBDOMAIN=your-subdomain


# ── Deployment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

WORKER_NAME=homestead
WORKER_URL=https://homestead.your-subdomain.workers.dev
HEALTH_URL=https://homestead.your-subdomain.workers.dev/health


# ── Your farm ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# A bearer secret: whoever holds the URL owns that farm, permanently. Farms are
# not registered anywhere — one is created on first contact with any key, so
# using a key claims it. Pick something unguessable and record it here, because
# there is no recovery if you lose it.
#
# Connector URL for Claude → Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector:
#   https://homestead.your-subdomain.workers.dev/mcp/<HOMESTEAD_FARM_KEY>
HOMESTEAD_FARM_KEY=


# ── GitHub ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Repository secrets the deploy workflow requires
# (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions):
#   CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
#   CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID
#
# Optional repository *variable*, only for a custom domain — the smoke test
# probes it instead of the workers.dev URL:
#   WORKER_URL


# ── Handy commands ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   Load into a shell:       set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#   Deploy by hand:          npm run deploy
#   Verify the token:        curl -s https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/user/tokens/verify \
#                              -H "Authorization: Bearer $CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN"
#   Re-set a GitHub secret:  printf '%s' "$CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN" | gh secret set CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
#   Check it is alive:       curl -s "$HEALTH_URL"
